Todd -

I have improved the program again (this time it only took 20 minutes
to make a MAJOR improvement).  Now, the program will handle alpha
input and return an "invalid entry" message.  Before it would blow
up.

Also, before, when you entered an incorrect/invalid value, you had to
wait until the program rebuilt the filelist... too time consuming!!!
I changed that so the program says "Please wait...  getting file
list" when it first gets the list of files in the variable... and, as
it gets the files, it sends the output to a temporary file.  Then, it
cats the files (numbers and filenames) to the screen.  If an invalid
entry is given, it simply prints "invalid entry" and re-cats the file
to the screen (instead of having to wait for the program to redo the
filelist).  MUCH BETTER!!!

Anyway, here it is... don't make too many major enhancements to it as
I have some other ideas to try on it (and I don't want us to work in
opposite directions)... let me know if you want it to perform
anything specific so I have some direction in the changes I make.
